  "regression_conclusion": "Confirmed source-level regression in b3eb1bcb relative to b02add36: it deleted the class_factory_viable guard and bracket-command caller, permitting unconditional quoted-container promotion. Pinned Java factory probes and the disabled-branch negative test confirm the expected behavior. No complete parent-revision parity benchmark was run; other removed mechanisms are diagnosed from the exact diff, not claimed as measured parent-to-child deltas.",
  "next_packet": {
    "mechanism": "shared container name/code grammar",
    "java": "CommandPackageWithUSymbol#getRegexConcat and executeArg: quoted DISPLAY as CODE, CODE as quoted DISPLAY, and bare name/code forms all feed the quark identity separately from display",
    "rust": "ClassParser::try_package at the campaign base rejects every non-package alias, cannot consume code-as-quoted-display, and therefore silently drops the group before its descendants. This explains why correct factory selection alone leaves many alias-bearing held-out examples failing.",
    "constraints": "Separate causal account and independent checker needed; do not bundle package shape expansion, quark endpoint ownership, or painted-bounds recovery into the same patch."
  },
